From 17b1ef7c9980571503f224279f27476712bd2650 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Lane A <lane-a@local.invalid>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:18:32 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] feat(live): long-running live recorder runner and gated
 clip finisher (tools)

- tools/live/record_live.py: record a live stream the user is authorised to
  clip into the rolling buffer, flag reactions with the fast voice pass, cut a
  window + quick preview per flag, status.json every tick.
- tools/live/finish_live.py: renders each flagged window with the gaming
  "face on top, game below" template, credit line and title; first checks the
  streamer is on camera AND moving at the reaction (on Twitch the game and mic
  share one track, so a voice flag can be game characters talking).
- tools/phase2/auto_edit.py: --select whole (edit an entire input window) and
  --hook-title.
Used on the Clix GTA VI marathon (authorised clipping campaign): 67 min
recorded, 28 flags, 11 finished clips, voice-only false flags rejected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
